    "finalMessage": "The film is written, but I could not run it in a browser: this session blocked launching a local server, Chrome and network access. It has only been syntax-checked and reviewed by reading every module, so \"no console errors\" and the look of each scene are unconfirmed until you open it.\n\n## Files\n\n```\nindex.html              entry point, import map for three@0.170.0 (jsDelivr)\nsrc/main.js             renderer, lights, table, play loop, ?t= freeze\nsrc/config.js           shared sizes and colours\nsrc/timeline.js         getState(t): cover angle, page turns, fold amount per world\nsrc/camera.js           keyframed camera path\nsrc/paper.js            paper helpers: cut-out cards, flat patches, pop-up hinges\nsrc/book.js             covers, page blocks, three turning leaves\nsrc/worlds/castle.js\nsrc/worlds/jungle.js\nsrc/worlds/port.js\nsrc/worlds/mountains.js\n```\n\n## How to view\n\nFrom this folder, with any static server:\n\n```\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/` for the looping film, or `http://localhost:8000/index.html?t=12.5` to freeze at a given second.\n\n## Timeline\n\n| Seconds | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| 0\u20131.5 | closed book on the table |\n| 1.5\u20133.5 | book opens |\n| 3\u20139 | castle |\n| 10\u201315.5 | jungle |\n| 16.5\u201322 | port with boats |\n| 23\u201328 | snowy peaks |\n| 28\u201329.5 | book closes |\n| 29.5\u201330 | closed book, camera back at its starting pose for the loop |\n\nPages turn between worlds, and each world folds flat before its page turns.\n\n## What to check first\n\n- **Console and first frame:** open the page once and look for errors; none of the Three.js calls have been executed.\n- **Each world at a frozen time:** `?t=6`, `?t=13`, `?t=19.5`, `?t=26` show the four worlds fully popped up.\n- **Geometry I corrected from reading alone:** hill silhouettes and battlements in the castle, sun height and vine arch in the jungle, wave strips and jib sail in the port, snow caps and sun height in the mountains. These are the likeliest places for something to still look off.\n\nThe modules were written by the crewlead worker model, since boss mode is on. My first batch went out with a placeholder instead of the interface contract and had to be redone, which cost about half an hour of worker time."
